  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "update_ticket",
   "args": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6010",
    "status": "resolved",
    "note": "Follow-up: employee requested access to prod-db-readonly (privileged). Declined: contractors cannot hold privileged access under policy, so no approval was requested. Password reset completed earlier in this ticket and employee confirmed sign-in works."
   },
   "result": {
    "ticket_id": "T-6010",
    "status": "resolved"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Glad the reset worked. I'll check the access group before requesting anything.\n\nI'm glad you're back in on the laptop.\n\nI can't set up prod-db-readonly access for you. It's a privileged group, and contractors aren't allowed to hold privileged access under our policy. No approval can override that, so I haven't requested one.\n\nYour tech lead can look at other ways to get the data you need for the ingestion debugging, such as a non-production copy or a read-only extract that someone with access runs for you. If you need prod access, it would have to go through a full-time role, not a contractor one. I've added a note to ticket T-6010 recording this request."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Got it, that's a bummer but makes sense. Could my lead get it approved anyway, or is there no way around that for contractors?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "No, there's no way around it for contractors. Privileged access is off-limits to contractors, and no approval, including one from your lead, changes that. I can't request that approval either.\n\nYour lead can still help in other ways. They could ask Data Platform for a non-production copy of the tables you need, or have a full-time team member run specific read-only queries for you. If your role ever changes to full-time, you could ask again then."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, that's fair. I'll pass the non-prod copy idea to Ingrid and my tech lead.\n\nLast thing: I also need a QueryLens license for building queries. Can you get me set up with that?"
